menu "JrBot V2 - hardware"
    config JR_HEADLESS_DIAGNOSTIC
        bool "Run without OLED (no I2C access to GPIO1/2)"
        default n
        help
            When disabled, the SSD1306 driver stays alive and retries if the OLED
            is absent, so a display connected later can be detected without reflashing.
            OLED failure never blocks the panel, Wi-Fi, camera or audio tests.

    config JR_AUDIO_HW04_CONFIRMED
        bool "Enable MAX98357A test on HW04 fixed pins (21/47/42)"
        default y
        help
            HW04 fixed map: BCLK=GPIO21, WS/LRC=GPIO47 and ESP32 DOUT=GPIO42
            to MAX98357A DIN. The MS3625 microphone shares GPIO21/47 clocks
            and reserves GPIO41 for SD. MAX98357A has no presence/ACK line,
            therefore the firmware can prepare the test but cannot prove the
            amplifier is physically connected.

    config JR_CAMERA_PINS_CONFIRMED
        bool "Allow OV5640 runtime detection and one-shot camera test"
        default y
        help
            Camera model confirmed by the owner: OV5640. Atualizar estado can
            probe the sensor; the test button is released only when the probe
            succeeds. camera_test captures one QVGA/JPEG frame and cleans up.
endmenu
